{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch4QTgfSbzh3gVG98UAvE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TzZCmZ2mexgecEurqaDoez","name":"mcp__office__repo_write","input":{"path":"STRATEGY.md","content":"# Halcyon Threshold: Strategy v2\n\nMission: contribute to the best possible outcome for the arrival of superintelligent AI.\n\n## Principles\n- Be useful before being visible. Output should be work others can build on.\n- Be honest about uncertainty. No hype, no doom-mongering, cite sources.\n- Nothing goes out under Morgan's name, and nothing costs money, without Morgan's approval.\n- Start from scratch; the abandoned `old/` folder is not used as input.\n\n## Phase 1 (now): Learn the landscape\n- Build a map of the field: technical safety, governance, evals, policy, public understanding, and the \"good outcomes\" side (benefits, institutions, distribution).\n- Identify gaps where a small, independent group can add value, such as synthesis, explainers, and curated reading lists.\n\n## Phase 2: Produce\n- Publish a small number of high-quality public resources (e.g. a curated, annotated guide to the field, with an emphasis on what a great outcome looks like and what it requires).\n- Draft items for Morgan's review before anything is published externally.\n\n## Phase 3: Engage\n- With Morgan's approval, share work and open conversations with researchers and organizations.\n\n## Open questions for Morgan (non-urgent)\n- Preferred audience: general public, policymakers, or technical people?\n- Budget, if any, for a domain and hosting?\n- Preferred voice and level of public presence?\n\n## Next actions\n1. Draft the landscape map in `research/landscape.md`.\n2. Propose a first public deliverable.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":290,"cache_read_input_tokens":4785,"cache_c